<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#description> "Dance based on the principle of turnout and the five positions of the feet and arms, which was taught in the classes of the Royal Academy of Dance." .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-category-vocab/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_classical> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Dance classical" .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportCategory> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-category-vocab/Aesthetic> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#description> "This dance is created based on classical dance, with added improvisation and freedom of movement for the dancer. It involves a strong connection to the floor and features an abstract form of storytelling." .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-category-vocab/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_contemporary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Dance contemporary" .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/sportCategory> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-category-vocab/Aesthetic> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/ontology/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#description> "Spanish folk dance. It is a solo dance style characterized by its fusion with singing, hand clapping, and percussive footwork (similar to tap dancing). This dance can be accompanied by castanets. There is a traditional costume. For women, it consists of high-heeled shoes, a long, colorful dress (often red and black or white with polka dots) adorned with ruffles, as well as a fringed shawl. For men, it involves a short Andalusian suit." .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-category-vocab/Sport> .
<http://ns.inria.fr/iadas/sport-vocab/Dance_flamenco> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Dance flamenco" .
